    <!-- Equalizer: additional options -->
    <string name="settings_eq_additional_options">Additional options</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_bass_boost_help_desc">What bass boost is</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_bass_boost_help_title">Bass boost</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_bass_boost_help_body">Unlike raising the equalizer\'s lowest band, this effect acts on the whole bass range, including frequencies lower than any band this device covers. On many phones it also adds harmonics so the bass can be felt even on small speakers that can\'t reproduce those low frequencies.</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_virtualizer_help_desc">What surround sound is</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_virtualizer_help_title">Surround sound</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_virtualizer_help_body">Widens the stereo image by simulating speakers placed off to the sides. It\'s not a volume adjustment by frequency: it mixes the left and right channels differently so the sound seems to come from outside your head. No equalizer slider can achieve this effect, since those only raise or lower frequency bands equally on both channels.</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_reverb_title">Reverb</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_reverb_help_desc">What reverb is</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_reverb_help_title">Reverb</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_reverb_help_body">Simulates the echo of a space (a room, a hall, an auditorium…) by adding delayed repetitions of the sound. It\'s an effect in time, not in frequency or stereo: neither the equalizer nor surround sound can create this sense of space. The dropdown picks the room size; \"None\" turns it off.</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_reverb_unsupported">Not supported on this device</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_dynamics_title">Dynamic range compressor</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_dynamics_help_desc">What the dynamic range compressor is</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_dynamics_help_title">Dynamic range compressor</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_dynamics_help_body">Unlike the volume booster, which raises the sound by a fixed amount, this effect reacts at every instant: it raises what sounds quiet and lowers what sounds loud, so the difference between them is smaller. It\'s useful for listening at low volume without losing the vocals, or for leveling songs mastered very differently. The higher the value, the more aggressive the compression.</string>
    <string name="settings_eq_dynamics_unsupported">Not supported on this device</string>

